<section id="about" class="about">
  <div class="container">
    <h6 class="about__title">About</h6>
    <div class="about__text">
      <p>
        I co-founded <a
          href="https://everythingincreation.com/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">Everything in Creation</a
        >, a design and development agency, and currently consult as a Design
        Engineer at <a
          href="https://www.humra.love/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">HUMRĀ</a
        >, a matchmaking and micro-wedding startup.
      </p>
      <p>
        My path here came through architectural visualization startups, where
        staying in one lane wasn't an option. I moved between Unreal Engine
        development, interface design, React applications, and mobile
        work—whatever the project needed. That experience taught me to learn
        fast and ship quickly, but more importantly, it showed me I didn't want
        to choose between design and development.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'm drawn to work that's visual and client-facing. I care about the
        details most people won't notice—the spacing, the consistency, the small
        interactions that accumulate into something that feels good to use. I
        take pride in having an eye for aesthetics and the technical skills to
        implement it properly. Design engineering feels like the first role that
        actually fits how I work.
      </p>
      <p>
        Outside of work, I'm learning to 3D model, hanging out with my two cats,
        and cataloging movies on <a
          href="https://letterboxd.com/mustafalazzawe/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">Letterboxd</a
        >.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

